 "description": "<p>Sermiligaaq (old spelling: Sermiligâq) is a settlement in the Sermersooq municipality in southeastern Greenland. Its population was 222 in 2010.[2] In Kalaallisut, its name means \"Beautiful Glacierfjord\".&nbsp;Source: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sermiligaaq\">Wikipedia</a></p><p>For further information (in Danish) see also the Danish Geodata Agency:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.gronlandskehavnelods.dk/#HID=deda928f-a690-4ecf-9f4d-8d495a90a132\">Den grønlandske Havnelods</a></p>",
